    "acceptance": [
      "When the Claude reviewer process exits non-zero and its standard output is a JSON envelope, either a single object or an event list with exactly one result event, that reports an error with a non-empty result, the raised launcher error keeps the existing process-failure wording and diagnostics location and additionally names the reported reason, bounded to its last 2000 characters.",
      "When the Claude reviewer process exits non-zero with non-JSON output, an envelope without an error flag or reason, or an event list without exactly one result event, the raised error is exactly the existing plain process-failure message with the diagnostics location.",
      "A non-zero reviewer exit always raises and never yields an answer, approval, retry or alternate engine; failures of the other engine keep their existing message, and the existing zero-exit error-envelope behavior is unchanged.",
      "On the release-versioned tree, where the only changes beyond the sealed correction are the package patch-version advance and the regenerated release and client manifests, the reviewer failure-reason behavior described by the existing criteria holds unchanged."
    ],
